<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Thailand</h1><p class="st-meta">1932 CE – present · capital Bangkok</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The only Southeast Asian state never colonised, a constitutional monarchy since 1932 whose politics have swung between elected governments and military rule.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The revolution of 24 June 1932 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khana-ratsadon">Khana Ratsadon</a>, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pridi-banomyong">Pridi Banomyong</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plaek-phibunsongkhram">Plaek Phibunsongkhram</a>, ended absolute monarchy in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/rattanakosin-kingdom">Rattanakosin Kingdom</a> and introduced a constitution. In 1939 Prime Minister Phibun changed the country's name from Siam to Thailand.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Thailand is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangkok">Bangkok</a> as its capital and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> as the main faith. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plaek-phibunsongkhram">Phibun</a> allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhumibol-adulyadej">Bhumibol Adulyadej</a>, who reigned from 1946 to 2016, became a powerful unifying figure. Military coups, including in 1947, 1957, 1976, 1991, 2006 and 2014, have repeatedly interrupted civilian rule. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> ally of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a>, it grew into a leading exporter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>, cars and electronics and a major tourist destination.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Thailand continues today under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vajiralongkorn">Vajiralongkorn</a>. It was a founding member of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/association-of-southeast-asian-nations">ASEAN</a> in 1967. Recent decades have been marked by political divisions, an insurgency in the Malay-Muslim south, and protests over the role of the military and monarchy.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/thailand.jpg" alt="Thailand" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Thailand.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1932 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bangkok</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Plaek Phibunsongkhram, Bhumibol Adulyadej, Vajiralongkorn</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Thai</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/thailand">Thailand</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Thailand, Siam</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1979&amp;focus=thailand" aria-label="Thailand on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7434 1666 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Thailand lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7754 1922L7754 1922"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7754 1922h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7754 1922h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7754 1922h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bangkok. <a href="/atlas?year=1979&amp;focus=thailand">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
